<section id="fun-with-ggcats" class="level2" data-number="12.2">
<h2 data-number="12.2" class="anchored" data-anchor-id="fun-with-ggcats"><span class="header-section-number">12.2</span> fun with ggcats</h2>
<p>The extra packages extend to the whimsical with the “cat plot”, brought to you by <a href="https://github.com/R-CoderDotCom/ggcats">ggcats</a></p>
<div class="cell">
<details class="code-fold">
<summary>Code</summary>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb115"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb115-1"><a href="#cb115-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">ggplot</span>(<span class="at">data=</span>gender_data_final, <span class="fu">aes</span>(<span class="at">x=</span>labor_m, <span class="at">y=</span>labor_f)) <span class="sc">+</span> <span class="fu">geom_cat</span>(<span class="at">cat =</span> <span class="st">"venus"</span>, <span class="at">size=</span><span class="dv">2</span>) <span class="sc">+</span> <span class="fu">geom_abline</span>(<span class="at">intercept =</span> <span class="dv">0</span>, <span class="at">slope =</span> <span class="dv">1</span>) <span class="sc">+</span> <span class="fu">labs</span>(<span class="at">x=</span><span class="st">"male labor participation (percent)"</span>, <span class="at">y=</span><span class="st">"female labor participation (percent)"</span>, <span class="at">title=</span><span class="st">"Comparing male and female labor participation"</span>) </span></code></pre></div><button title="Copy to Clipboard" class="code-copy-button"><i class="bi"></i></button></div>
</details>
<div class="cell-output-display">
<div>
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="data_visualization_1_files/figure-html/cat%20plot-1.png" class="img-fluid figure-img" width="672"></p>
</figure>
</div>
</div>
<details class="code-fold">
<summary>Code</summary>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb116"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb116-1"><a href="#cb116-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># also try "nyancat", "grumpy", "pusheen"</span></span></code></pre></div><button title="Copy to Clipboard" class="code-copy-button"><i class="bi"></i></button></div>
</details>
</div>
<p>And a second example illustrating using different cats to represent different data elements. This is a quick example using the built-in <em>iris</em> dataset.</p>
<div class="cell">
<details class="code-fold">
<summary>Code</summary>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb117"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb117-1"><a href="#cb117-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># Create a new column</span></span>
<span id="cb117-2"><a href="#cb117-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>iris<span class="sc">$</span>cat <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">factor</span>(iris<span class="sc">$</span>Species,</span>
<span id="cb117-3"><a href="#cb117-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                   <span class="at">labels =</span> <span class="fu">c</span>(<span class="st">"pusheen"</span>, <span class="st">"toast"</span>,</span>
<span id="cb117-4"><a href="#cb117-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                              <span class="st">"venus"</span>))</span>
<span id="cb117-5"><a href="#cb117-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a></span>
<span id="cb117-6"><a href="#cb117-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># Scatter plot by group</span></span>
<span id="cb117-7"><a href="#cb117-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">ggplot</span>(iris, <span class="fu">aes</span>(Petal.Length, Petal.Width)) <span class="sc">+</span></span>
<span id="cb117-8"><a href="#cb117-8" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a> <span class="fu">geom_cat</span>(<span class="fu">aes</span>(<span class="at">cat =</span> cat), <span class="at">size =</span> <span class="dv">4</span>)</span></code></pre></div><button title="Copy to Clipboard" class="code-copy-button"><i class="bi"></i></button></div>
</details>
<div class="cell-output-display">
<div>
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="data_visualization_1_files/figure-html/cat%20plot%202-1.png" class="img-fluid figure-img" width="672"></p>
</figure>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
